Ideally, each letter should have certain properties which all monsters
of that category share, and not too many monster types in it. It's not
that weird that gnomes and dwarves are different: gnomes are neutral,
dwarves are lawful; G are small, h are medium. It's the bugbear which is
in the wrong group, really, but yes, so are flayers.
The real problem is that the categories are, by necessity, decided on a
lot of different criteria. Size and alignment; but also special attacks,
other properties such as poison, and even real-life species. And you
can't really get around this, because you _do_ want all kobolds
together, and ideally not with the gnomes.

